@test("ngspice: a 5 v supply from the wall: transformer, bridge, reservoir and a series regulator")
oracle_wall_supply()
    val netlist = """
        A 5 V supply from the wall: transformer, bridge, reservoir and a series regulator
        * examples/wallwart.amber as a netlist. 120 V at 60 Hz stepped down to 9 V by a transformer, rectified
        * by a bridge of four diodes into a 1000 uF reservoir, and held at 5 V by a pass transistor whose base
        * an error amplifier steers, comparing a share of the output with a 3.3 V zener. Switched on at a zero
        * crossing with every capacitor empty.
        *
        * RI and RC are the transformer's insulation and core losses, which a schematic's transformer has
        * built in. Without RI the secondary has nothing to say where it stands while all four diodes are off,
        * and ngspice and amber both give up at about 6.4 ms.
        VM line 0 SIN(0 170 60)
        RP line p 12
        LP p 0 10
        RC p 0 10k
        LS s1 s2 56.25m
        K1 LP LS 0.999
        RI s2 0 1g
        RW s1 a 0.3
        D1 a raw d1n4148
        D2 s2 raw d1n4148
        D3 0 a d1n4148
        D4 0 s2 d1n4148
        CF raw 0 1000u
        RB raw base 1k
        Q1 raw base out q2n3904
        Q2 base fb ref q2n3904
        RZ out ref 1k
        DZ 0 ref dz3v3
        R1 out fb 2.7k
        R2 fb 0 10k
        RL out 0 100
        RLED out led 1k
        DLED led 0 dred
        .model d1n4148 D (IS=2.52n N=1.752 RS=0.568)
        .model dz3v3 D (IS=1e-14 N=1 RS=2 BV=3.3 IBV=5m)
        .model dred D (IS=1e-17 N=2 RS=2)
        .model q2n3904 NPN (IS=6.734f BF=416.4 BR=0.7371 VAF=74.03)
        .tran 0.2m 100m
        .control
        option reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-14 vntol=1e-9
        tran 0.2m 100m 0 10u
        linearize v(s1) v(raw) v(out)
        wrdata wall_supply.data v(s1) v(raw) v(out)
        .endc
        .end
        """
    val names = ["v(s1)", "v(raw)", "v(out)"]
    val expected = [
